  "narration": {
    "title": "The Arms Race: Milwaukee Sets the Pace",
    "intro": "Today the pitching gets its own spotlight. Milwaukee has both the best rotation and Jacob Misiorowski, who is still sitting on a form score of 100. Around him, a few strong arms are cooling while a couple of Mariners are heating up.",
    "staff_lead": "Milwaukee's rotation leads at a 3.22 ERA, a step ahead of Tampa Bay (3.31) and the Dodgers (3.34). The top three sit close enough that a couple of starts could reshuffle them, but the Brewers have held the front for a while now.",
    "bullpen_lead": "Atlanta's relievers own the top spot at a 3.07 ERA, with the Yankees right on their heels at 3.09. After that there's a small gap to Boston (3.38), so the Braves and Yankees are in a class of their own for late-inning work.",
    "arms_lead": "Misiorowski remains untouchable at a 1.47 ERA and a 0.78 WHIP, the only arm at a perfect 100. Behind him, Cam Schlittler (2.01 ERA) and Yoshinobu Yamamoto (2.49) round out the leaders, with Yamamoto the one still trending up.",
    "risers_lead": "Seattle supplies both climbers: Logan Gilbert rose five to a form of 75 and Emerson Hancock added four to reach 72. On the other side, Logan Webb slid 11 points to 61 and Paul Skenes dropped seven to 68 \u2014 still good arms, just a rougher stretch."
  }
